---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Safeguarding & complaints"
  description="Safeguarding commitments and how to raise a concern or complaint with Therapy With Ben, the HCPC, or the NCIP."
>
  <p class="policy-intro">
    This policy outlines statutory safeguarding commitments, professional standards, and
    clear routes for raising concerns or formal complaints — including signposting to
    professional regulators. It applies to Therapy With Ben (Ben Richardson, sole trader;
    trading name of That Music Therapy Lot).
  </p>

  <h2>Part 1: Safeguarding statement &amp; commitment</h2>

  <h3>1. Duty of care &amp; training</h3>
  <p>
    As a sole practitioner, maintaining client safety and welfare is central to my practice.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Safeguarding training:</strong> I maintain up-to-date, accredited safeguarding
      training appropriate for working with adults, young people, and vulnerable populations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>DBS status:</strong> I am registered with the Disclosure and Barring Service
      (DBS) Update Service (Certificate No. <strong>001788330063</strong>), allowing
      real-time verification of my enhanced background checks.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. Safeguarding thresholds &amp; confidentiality</h3>
  <p>
    All therapeutic sessions are confidential. However, confidentiality may be overridden
    if a safeguarding threshold is met. This occurs when:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>There is a demonstrable risk of serious harm to yourself or another person.</li>
    <li>
      A child, young person, or vulnerable adult is identified as suffering or at risk of
      suffering significant harm.
    </li>
    <li>
      Disclosure is required by law (for example severe criminal acts, terrorism, or a
      court order).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Wherever safe and legally permissible, any necessary safeguarding referral to external
    agencies (such as Social Care or emergency services) will be discussed with you before
    information is shared.
  </p>

  <h2>Part 2: Complaints &amp; fitness to practice</h2>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with any aspect of your care, communication, or service, you have
    the right to raise a concern. I aim to address issues transparently and professionally.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Informal resolution (Stage 1)</h3>
  <p>
    If you feel comfortable doing so, I encourage you to raise any concerns directly with
    me during or between sessions. Many misunderstandings or misalignments in therapy can
    be resolved through open clinical discussion. You can also contact
    {' '}<a href="mailto:hello@therapywithben.uk">hello@therapywithben.uk</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Regulatory &amp; professional body complaints (Stage 2)</h3>
  <p>
    If a concern cannot be resolved informally, or if your complaint relates to
    professional misconduct, ethics, or fitness to practice, you can escalate your
    complaint directly to the relevant professional registering bodies.
  </p>

  <h3>A. Statutory regulation: Health and Care Professions Council (HCPC)</h3>
  <p>
    I am registered as a clinician with the HCPC. Regardless of the specific modality used
    in your sessions (including integrative psychotherapy), you retain the right to raise
    a concern regarding my overall fitness to practice with the HCPC at any time.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Scope:</strong> Professional conduct, ethical breaches, competence, and public safety.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How to lodge a concern:</strong>
      <a href="https://www.hcpc-uk.org/concerns/raising-concerns/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        HCPC — Raising concerns
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B. Professional body: National Council of Integrative Psychotherapists (NCIP)</h3>
  <p>
    For concerns specifically relating to the delivery or ethical framework of integrative
    psychotherapy, you can complain to the NCIP.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Scope:</strong> Breaches of the NCIP Code of Ethics and Psychotherapy Standards.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How to lodge a complaint:</strong> via the
      {' '}<a href="https://www.the-ncip.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NCIP website</a>
      {' '}or email
      {' '}<a href="mailto:complaints@the-ncip.com">complaints@the-ncip.com</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related policies</h2>
  <p>
    See also the
    {' '}<a href="/therapeutic-agreement">Therapeutic agreement</a>,
    {' '}<a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy policy</a>, and
    {' '}<a href="/payment-policy">Payment &amp; cancellation policy</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
